  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "A circle is inscribed in a square of side $x$, then a square is inscribed in that circle, a circle is inscribed in the latter square, and so on. If $S_n$ is the sum of the areas of the first $n$ circles so inscribed, then $\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}S_n$",
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\frac{\\pi x^2}{4}$",
    "B": "$\\frac{\\pi x^2}{3}$",
    "C": "$\\frac{\\pi x^2}{2}$",
    "D": "$\\pi x^2$"
  },
  "answer": "C",
